● BEN Bridge Engine Development Summary

  Current Project Status

  Objective: Performance optimization and compatibility improvements for the BEN bridge engine, specifically focusing on model
  inference speed and configuration flexibility.

  Recent Key Changes

  1. Single Dummy Lead Model Optimization (src/botopeninglead.py:413)

  - Issue: Incompatibility between 24-card bidding models and 32-card single dummy (SD) models
  - Solution: Added automatic format conversion logic
  - Impact: Enables using faster 24-card bidding models with existing 32-card SD models
  - Code: Converts hands from 24-card to 32-card format using deck52.handxxto52str() and binary.parse_hand_f(32)()

  2. TensorFlow Performance Optimization (src/nn/lead_singledummy_tf2.py:14)

  - Issue: Slow model inference due to model.predict() overhead
  - Solution: Direct model calls using model(x, training=False)
  - Impact: ~2-3x faster inference for single dummy lead evaluation
  - Removed: @tf.function decorator that was causing compilation delays

  3. API Server Architecture Changes (src/gameapi.py:3)

  - Issue: Thread safety problems with gevent and TensorFlow
  - Solution: Removed gevent monkey patching, added TF thread limiting
  - Configuration: Limited TF to 1 inter/intra-op thread to prevent contention
  - Deployment: Switched from gevent WSGIServer to Flask dev server (with gunicorn recommendation)

  4. Configuration Strategy Shift

  - Previous: Full production configuration with extensive search and sampling
  - Current: Minimal search configuration for speed optimization
  - Active Config: minimal_search_api.conf (vs production_api.conf)
  - Key Changes:
    - Search thresholds: 0.90 (effectively disabled vs 0.10-0.03)
    - Sampling: 10 hands (vs 100 hands)
    - Double dummy: disabled (vs enabled)
    - PIMC: disabled (vs enabled)

